From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] ui-egui: phone layout hook (top row, contextual bottom toolbar) and phone-sized dialogs

Phase 6 WP6 (docs/phase6/PLAN.md section 5.1). A window at most 600 CSS px wide whose last pointer was a finger gets a phone layout instead of the title bar, the ribbon, the status bar and the panes: the extension (docs-office, domains/docs/crates/docs-office/src/phone.rs) draws a 48 dp top row and a contextual 48 dp bottom toolbar with sheets and returns the commands to run, which `phone_chrome` runs with `WordApp::run`. Entering it shows the document in Web Layout and leaving restores the view; the selection mini toolbar yields to the touch action bar (0139); a dialog is at most the screen wide and scrolls inside; a shrinking window (soft keyboard) scrolls the caret into view. The hook is set only by the web app (`set_phone`), so the desktop apps and a build without the extension are unchanged: `phone_chrome` returns false at once.
---
 crates/ui-egui/src/office_overlay.rs | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/ui-egui/src/office_overlay.rs b/crates/ui-egui/src/office_overlay.rs
index ba7c209..42014f9 100644
--- a/crates/ui-egui/src/office_overlay.rs
+++ b/crates/ui-egui/src/office_overlay.rs
@@ -159,8 +159,7 @@ static PHONE_H: std::sync::atomic::AtomicU32 = std::sync::atomic::AtomicU32::new
 static PHONE_VIEW: Mutex<Option<(wordcraft_engine::layout::ViewMode, bool)>> = Mutex::new(None);
 
 /// The phone layout's labels upstream has no catalog row for, as literals so `cargo xt i18n extract` sees them (docs-office looks every label up by key).
-#[allow(dead_code)]
-fn phone_labels() -> [&'static str; 3] {
+pub fn phone_labels() -> [&'static str; 3] {
     [tl!("Keyboard"), tl!("More"), tl!("Desktop layout")]
 }
 
